MIRROR LICENSE v1.0
"You Get What You Give"

Preamble
This license operates on a single principle: reciprocity.
The terms under which you may use this software are determined by the terms under which you license your own software to others. The license class you apply to your recipients becomes the license class applied to you.

Article 1: The Mirror Clause
1.1 The licensee's effective license terms are determined by the most restrictive license the licensee applies to their own distributed software or services.
1.2 If the licensee distributes software under AGPLv3, they receive this software under AGPLv3-equivalent terms.
1.3 If the licensee distributes software under GPL, they receive this software under GPL-equivalent terms.
1.4 If the licensee distributes software under MIT, Apache 2.0, or equivalent permissive terms, they receive this software under the same permissive terms.
1.5 If the licensee distributes proprietary software with no source disclosure, they receive this software under a non-commercial research-only license: they may use it internally and study it, but may not distribute derivative works commercially without publishing their own source.

Article 2: Determination of License Class
2.1 The licensee's license class is determined by the license terms of their most widely distributed software product or service as of the date of first use.
2.2 If the licensee distributes multiple products under different licenses, the most restrictive license applies.
2.3 If the licensee has no publicly distributed software, they are classified as Permissive by default.
2.4 If the licensee distributes "open-core" software where the free tier is intentionally limited to force commercial purchase, they are classified as Restrictive regardless of the named license.

Article 3: The Sovereignty Exception
3.1 Any licensee who can demonstrate that their software:
(a) Boots on bare metal without a host operating system
(b) Contains zero third-party runtime dependencies
(c) Includes SHA-256 cryptographic verification of all components
(d) Runs entirely offline with no telemetry or cloud dependency

...is automatically classified as Permissive, regardless of their named license, and receives this software under 0BSD terms.

Article 4: Enforcement
4.1 This license is self-enforcing through social and legal reciprocity.
4.2 A licensee who misrepresents their license class to obtain more permissive terms forfeits all rights granted herein.
4.3 Disputes are resolved through public documentation and community verification, not private arbitration.

Article 5: No Warranty
5.1 This software is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind.
5.2 The mirror clause is a philosophical statement of reciprocity. Its enforceability in any jurisdiction is the licensee's responsibility to verify.

Final Clause
"You get what you give. You treat your users with transparency — you receive transparency. You treat your users with traps — you receive traps."

